WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.970
Twenty fifth November, nineteen

2
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.230
forty nine.

3
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.900
Doctor Ambedkar has three

4
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.300
warnings for the Constituent

5
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.100
Assembly.

6
00:00:07.691 --> 00:00:08.431
His worry:

7
00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:10.631
a democracy can keep its form,

8
00:00:10.631 --> 00:00:13.091
yet become a dictatorship.

9
00:00:13.091 --> 00:00:15.171
Three things must be done,

10
00:00:15.171 --> 00:00:17.381
numbered like an exam paper.

11
00:00:17.958 --> 00:00:19.558
First: hold fast to

12
00:00:19.558 --> 00:00:21.018
constitutional methods.

13
00:00:21.018 --> 00:00:23.038
Where such paths are open, give

14
00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:24.618
up revolution, civil

15
00:00:24.618 --> 00:00:26.878
disobedience, non cooperation

16
00:00:26.878 --> 00:00:27.878
and satyagraha.

17
00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:29.648
The grammar of anarchy.

18
00:00:30.218 --> 00:00:33.118
Second: never lay your liberties

19
00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:34.898
at the feet of even a great

20
00:00:34.898 --> 00:00:37.418
man. No nation can be grateful

21
00:00:37.418 --> 00:00:39.248
at the cost of its liberty.

22
00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:41.776
In India, he says, devotion to

23
00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:43.796
leaders matters more in politics

24
00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:44.936
than anywhere.

25
00:00:44.936 --> 00:00:47.196
In religion, bhakti may bring

26
00:00:47.196 --> 00:00:49.636
salvation. In politics, a sure

27
00:00:49.636 --> 00:00:51.106
road to dictatorship.

28
00:00:51.906 --> 00:00:54.766
Third: political democracy needs

29
00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:56.906
social democracy beneath it.

30
00:00:56.906 --> 00:00:59.456
Liberty, equality, fraternity.

31
00:01:00.173 --> 00:01:01.953
On the twenty sixth of January,

32
00:01:01.953 --> 00:01:04.013
he says, India enters a life of

33
00:01:04.013 --> 00:01:05.993
contradictions: equality in

34
00:01:05.993 --> 00:01:08.153
politics, inequality in social

35
00:01:08.153 --> 00:01:09.683
and economic life.

36
00:01:10.414 --> 00:01:11.874
How long shall we continue to

37
00:01:11.874 --> 00:01:12.934
live this life of

38
00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.094
contradictions? Too long, he

39
00:01:15.094 --> 00:01:17.174
warns, and political democracy

40
00:01:17.174 --> 00:01:18.524
is in peril.

41
00:01:19.824 --> 00:01:20.591
For GS2:

42
00:01:20.591 --> 00:01:23.764
constitutional methods, no hero

43
00:01:23.764 --> 00:01:25.934
worship, social democracy.

44
00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:29.569
Form is easy to keep.

45
00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:31.319
Substance takes work.
